    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "TIT",
      "chapter": 2,
      "chapter_usfm": "TIT.2",
      "version_id": 68,
      "version_abbr": "GNT",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.1",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "But you must teach what agrees with sound doctrine."
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.2",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Instruct the older men to be sober, sensible, and self-controlled; to be sound in their faith, love, and endurance."
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.3",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "In the same way instruct the older women to behave as women should who live a holy life. They must not be slanderers or slaves to wine. They must teach what is good,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.4",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "in order to train the younger women to love their husbands and children,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.5",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "to be self-controlled and pure, and to be good housewives who submit themselves to their husbands, so that no one will speak evil of the message that comes from God."
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "In the same way urge the young men to be self-controlled."
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.7",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "In all things you yourself must be an example of good behavior. Be sincere and serious in your teaching."
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.8",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Use sound words that cannot be criticized, so that your enemies may be put to shame by not having anything bad to say about us."
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.9",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Slaves are to submit themselves to their masters and please them in all things. They must not talk back to them"
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.10",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "or steal from them. Instead, they must show that they are always good and faithful, so as to bring credit to the teaching about God our Savior in all they do."
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.11",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For God has revealed his grace for the salvation of all people."
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.12",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "That grace instructs us to give up ungodly living and worldly passions, and to live self-controlled, upright, and godly lives in this world,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.13",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "as we wait for the blessed Day we hope for, when the glory of our great God and Savior Jesus Christ will appear."
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.14",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "He gave himself for us, to rescue us from all wickedness and to make us a pure people who belong to him alone and are eager to do good."
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.15",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Teach these things and use your full authority as you encourage and rebuke your hearers. Let none of them look down on you."
        }
      ],
      "verse_count": 15,
      "headings": [],
      "footnotes": [
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "TIT.2.13",
          "note_ref": "2.13:",
          "note_type": "footnote",
          "references": [],
          "text": "our great God and Savior Jesus Christ; or the great God and our Savior Jesus Christ."
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
